  "body": "**Blocked by:** #104\n\n## Context\n\nAn agent may propose processing but must never hold authority to write a destination directly.\n\n## Task\n\nRestrict Semprec's agent grant to creating/updating Processing proposals; omit target database/page write grants. Implement user-context actions `POST /api/proposals/:id/confirm`, `/reject`, and `/revise`. Confirm is the sole cross-destination path: for `database`, call the generic create-item choke point; for `pageContent`, call the existing block-append mechanism. Persist `resultItemId` and `resultLabel`, then lock as confirmed. Reject writes no target and locks as rejected. Revise accepts `{message}`, appends history, and may replace the complete proposal including `entityKind`; partial patch semantics are forbidden. Make transitions atomic and deterministic under duplicate requests. Authentication enforcement is retrofitted by the later auth batch; no circular dependency is introduced here.\n\n## Scope\n\n### In scope\n\n- Grant separation, three actions, transition validation, target execution, and result linkage.\n\n### Out of scope\n\n- Auth implementation and direct AI target writes.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- An agent cannot call target writes through its grant.\n- Confirm executes one generic destination write and is idempotent under retry.\n- Reject never writes a destination.\n- Revise can switch database to page content atomically and records the conversation.\n",
